    "description": "An operations console combines modules for fleet telemetry, map display, alarm workflows, incident records, and audit reporting. Telemetry sources publish readings, workflow changes publish alarm transitions, and several modules consume both kinds of notifications. Modules are loaded and unloaded independently during rolling deployments. Today, every consumer locates every relevant source, registers separately, and duplicates cleanup logic, so a newly deployed module can begin receiving traffic before its dependencies are ready and shutdown can leave stale subscriptions. The console needs a single registration boundary that accepts source and consumer descriptions, owns the wiring and cleanup, and routes notifications without making telemetry or workflow modules aware of the specific displays and recorders attached to them. Registration failures must be isolated and observable rather than preventing unrelated modules from connecting.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose how notifications from multiple changing sources reach multiple independently deployed consumers without duplicating pairwise registration and cleanup.",
    "notes": "Event-aggregator fits because one hub owns subscription wiring and cleanup across independently deployed sources and consumers without pairwise registration; observer and publisher-subscriber are the near-miss siblings and mediator supports coordination."
  },
